      "name": null,
      "problem": "What are the solutions of the equation $(x+1)^{2}=-25?$",
      "worked_solution": "The left-hand side is a perfect square. Therefore, we can solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)^{2} & =-25 \\\\ x+1 & =\\pm \\sqrt{-25} \\\\ x+1 & =\\pm 5\\,\\text{i} \\\\ x & =-1\\pm 5\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has two solutions, $x=-1+5\\,\\text{i}$ and $x=-1-5\\,\\text{i}.$",
